{"kind":"event","event_id":2427,"event_uid":"01M2J21PGHHTWHN56TMM6YN1WF","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":131,"issue_uid":"01M2J1YJ2W2V6V1X0NQRDZ02BZ","issue_short_id":"02bz","actor":"impl:1@run-8","hlc_physical_ms":1789460011537,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"b02be243c199cb186df60e982228245e1da65a545378c323222499edb67d2cdd","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2J21PGG0HXK652AXJJTT8GK","author":"impl:1@run-8","body":"run-8 task 1: writing the two interaction exams (click-completes-todo, enter-submits-todo), the new expected file two-todos-first-done.json (row 0 done — the run-7 park was the BASE two-todos-one-done.json, which has row 1 done), and the README '## State exams' section. Reusing state-exams/expected/one-open-todo.json for the Enter exam rather than creating a second file. interaction-evidence.test.ts is the peer's exam and is not mine to write.","created_at":"2026-09-15T08:13:31.536872399Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T08:13:31.537Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2428,"event_uid":"01M2J22EXPRPF4QTNFCXCFJYN6","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":131,"issue_uid":"01M2J1YJ2W2V6V1X0NQRDZ02BZ","issue_short_id":"02bz","actor":"exam:1@run-8","hlc_physical_ms":1789460036534,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"c4a0410481b759762e023c779c9d7372c4bb04dea0e97a91311cc22beb840e8f","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2J22EXMNBD3QGT4FTCS7JSH","author":"exam:1@run-8","body":"examiner (run-8, task 1): writing tests/state-exams/interaction-evidence.test.ts only. Approach: the exam never imports the two interaction exams — it spawns one child `bun test <file>` per exam from the repo root, each with its own fresh mkdtemp ULTRA_RUN_DIR and with ULTRA_TASK/ULTRA_EXAM_PASS deleted from the child env, so the record lands at state-exams/task-none/<stem>-none. Each child run is memoised in a module-level promise so legs (a)+(c) share one click run and legs (b)+(c) one Enter run; every test that touches a child carries an explicit long timeout (bun's 5s default would kill a real browser run). Legs (a)/(b) read the two exam files as text and match quote-tolerant regexes over the object literals the Machine clauses name (click selector, the two view entries, the mutant edit; for the Enter exam the type entry's index before the key entry's, and 'Enter' inside the key entry). Leg (d) writes tests/state-exams/tmp-red-<pid>.test.ts from the click exam's text with two-todos-first-done.json -> still-empty.json, spawns it, asserts non-zero exit plus 'store move: expected state not reached' on the combined output, and unlinks in a finally. Leg (e) runs the third Run: line verbatim through bash, then the same pipeline against a copy of README.md with the '## State exams' section spliced out, asserting non-zero.","created_at":"2026-09-15T08:13:56.532892252Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T08:13:56.534Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2429,"event_uid":"01M2J24X6ENXHED0CMTSTH9WQB","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":131,"issue_uid":"01M2J1YJ2W2V6V1X0NQRDZ02BZ","issue_short_id":"02bz","actor":"impl:1@run-8","hlc_physical_ms":1789460116686,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"9ea2ac43797bfafa306474b0f642dd2c1d6abdf233a014a4dc8d6c731eb0144d","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2J24X6C1WQRQGXK7T6XK0SG","author":"impl:1@run-8","body":"run-8 task 1 done. All four PROOFS green on this tree: both exams pass (bun test, real Chromium at /headless-shell/headless-shell, ~1.2s and ~1.5s), the README grep exits 0, typecheck exits 0.\n\nVerified the peer exam's other legs by hand too:\n- M3 click: ULTRA_RUN_DIR child run leaves state-exams/task-none/click-completes-todo-none/ with exactly the six files; store-diff.json []; walls browser 'ran', action_ms 80.5; mutant killed:true path todos/0/completed; dom.html has class=\"todoItem completed\" and data-checked=\"true\"; screenshot.png starts 89504e47.\n- M3 enter: same six files under enter-submits-todo-none/; store-diff []; walls.browser 'ran'; mutant killed:true path todos/0/text.\n- M4: a sed copy of the click exam with still-empty.json as expected exits 1 and prints 'store move: expected state not reached'.\n- M5 negative: README with the '## State exams' section stripped makes the pipeline exit 1.\n\nDecisions a later session would otherwise rediscover: (1) two-todos-first-done.json is row 0 done / row 1 open — the BASE two-todos-one-done.json is the mirror of it and is what parked run-7; (2) the Enter exam reuses the BASE one-open-todo.json, no second expected file was created; (3) both specs carry store: () => createTodosStore() because the task's Context spells that shape, even though browserStoreMove ignores spec.store for the interaction form — it is inert, not load-bearing; (4) the click view uses .todoItem.completed input[type=checkbox], since assertView's allRead requires every match to read data-checked=\"true\" and the bare selector matches both boxes. interaction-evidence.test.ts is the peer's exam and was not written here.","created_at":"2026-09-15T08:15:16.684790902Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T08:15:16.686Z"}
